  "text": "She touched his coat in a crowd and stopped the whole procession. Mark chapter five. Twelve years of bleeding. And Mark, who was not gentle about it, says she had suffered many things of many physicians, and had spent all that she had, and was nothing bettered, but rather grew worse. Every doctor paid. Every option gone. Worse than when she started. Then she hears about Jesus. And she does not go to the front and ask. She comes up behind him in the press of the crowd, because she says within herself, if I may touch but his clothes, I shall be whole. And she does. And straightway the fountain of her blood was dried up. And here is the part that always gets me. He stops. In a crowd pressing in on him from every side, he turns around and asks who touched my clothes. His disciples think that is an absurd question. But he keeps looking. And she comes fearing and trembling, and falls down, and tells him all the truth. Not a summary. All of it. And he says, daughter, thy faith hath made thee whole. Go in peace. He would not let her leave as a secret.",
